# Usage (keep quality, cut waste)

## Process

- Prefer Agent for small, decision-locked tasks; Plan only for multi-file trade-offs or unclear scope
- If an attached plan’s todos are already done in the repo, say so in 1–2 lines and stop — do not re-implement
- Do not recreate todos that already exist; do not edit plan files unless asked
- Search/read the few known files first; avoid broad explore agents for needle lookups
- Reuse `js/shared/` modules (auth, premium, nav, skeleton) — do not invent parallel systems

## Replies

- Lead with the answer or status; no task restatement or process narration
- Keep user-facing text short; expand only when asked or when trade-offs need a decision
- Skip “what we didn’t do” and long test-plan essays unless the user needs them

## Quality (do not weaken)

- Still read before edit; match existing patterns; finish the requested work
- Still follow purpose / design / supabase / project rules for real product decisions
